@@ -0,0 +1,580 @@
+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] up: L1515 cheaper report lookups, frees and locks (EDEN_UP_L1515_QUERY_CHEAP, off unless set)
+
+Ports zortos293/Lichii #1515, 5b9012f (author Zortos; from #1161), read by hand onto our query
+cache (0446/0447/0560/0706 and the split). Gated by EDEN_UP_L1515_QUERY_CHEAP (exact "1"), read
+once at boot; off by default. Not built or measured with this tree yet. Upstream measured at
+Ocarina of Time's water: 51.2/51.9 fps against 49.8/51.4, 4.61/4.60 us of back thread per draw
+against 4.97/4.83 (their PC, not the PS5).
+
+On:
+- BankBase: references are two counters, `added` (GPU thread) and `dropped` (fencing thread), each
+  on its own cache line; References() = added - dropped (ASSERT on a double free).
+- UnregisterPending: the queries leave the cache under cache_mutex, then each streamer frees its
+  batch under its own lock once (StreamerInterface::FreeMany; SimpleStreamer and SamplesStreamer
+  override it).
+- SimpleStreamer::BuildQuery: the building thread takes free ids from its own `reusable` list,
+  refilled from the freed list (oldest first) under the lock once per batch. Not in upstream: the
+  first building thread owns the list; a build from any other thread (not expected) takes a new
+  slot under the lock, counts foreign_build, and the owner then builds under the lock too. With the
+  switch the free ids go to spare_queries (EDEN_UP_REPORT_NO_ALLOC's FIFO is not used).
+- InvalidateRegion, SemiFlushRegion, HasCachedReports, IsRegionGpuModified skip pages on which no
+  report was ever registered (page_filter). The filter exists only with
+  EDEN_NX2_INVALIDATION_FILTER=1 (page_filter.h); without it Any answers true and nothing skips.
+- IterateCache: a range of up to 32 candidate start offsets looks those offsets up instead of
+  walking every query of the page. Same queries; our EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_PR700 early-exit rule kept.
+Always (layout only, no behaviour): host_results and last_used_tick of SamplesQueryBank on lines
+of their own; BankBase's two new counters (+~192 bytes per bank).
+
+Not taken: upstream's unit test (src/tests); upstream's page_filter check in a report-range
+function our tree does not have (its 16-byte look-back variant).
+Count lines (each logs at 1, 2, 4, ...): "EDEN_UP_L1515_QUERY_CHEAP count free_batches= /
+freed_queries= / filter_skips= / probes= / id_refills= / foreign_build=". Boot line when on.
+Memory: per-streamer scratch vectors and the reusable id list (a few KiB); no GPU memory.
+
+No file here is a translation id input and no name is added to TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.
