+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_L1520_WORDS_POOL and EDEN_UP_L1520_ASYNC_COPY (zortos293/Lichii #1520, off unless set)
+
+Port of zortos293/Lichii #1520 (8dcea11bf62fd8ad9885955280afbe2e2931819e, Zortos, co-authors
+Lucas Borges and Copilot; from #1161): "dma_pusher: reuse command list copies and copy them again
+off the front at resumes". Upstream measured at Ocarina of Time's water (PC, 3 runs): 62.4 ->
+63.8 fps; the split front's busy time 726 -> 671 ms/s; the back waiting for the front 92 -> 54 ms/s.
+Not measured on the PS5.
+
+What (two switches, each off unless set to exactly "1"):
+- EDEN_UP_L1520_WORDS_POOL=1: CommandList::submitted_words takes its blocks from
+  CommandWordsPool, which keeps freed blocks (4 KiB to 4 MiB, by size class) for the next
+  submission instead of the guest's submit thread allocating and the GPU thread freeing ~1000
+  a second. EDEN_UP_L1520_WORDS_POOL_MIB (default 48, upstream's classes add up to ~48) caps
+  what is kept in all. Memory: up to that many MiB of heap stay held while blocks are free; they
+  go back when a channel goes away (~DmaPusher Trim). Line every 10 s while blocks are asked
+  for: "EDEN_UP_L1520_WORDS_POOL: ... asked for, ... reused, ... kept, ... freed, ... MiB kept".
+- EDEN_UP_L1520_ASYNC_COPY=1: at a resume after a semaphore acquire, the lists queued after the
+  one the parse resumes in are copied again on a "GPUSnapshot" thread (256-job ring); the GPU
+  thread waits for a list's copy when it reaches it (Step), before a synchronous refresh of it,
+  before any non-list command (maps, flushes, ticks: the copier reads through the channel's
+  memory manager), at shutdown (in GpuSplit::Stop, as upstream's NotifyShutdown wait: the PS5
+  front rewrites NotifyShutdown's text) and when a channel goes away. Before the copies the split's
+  front publishes what it sent. Only where this tree's refresh of those lists is a plain copy of
+  memory: not with EDEN_NX2_DESYNC_FIX, EDEN_UP_RESUME_KEEP_COPY or EDEN_NX2_FETCH_COUNT (their
+  per-entry judging stays on the GPU thread); the refresh check's walk and log end at the first
+  queued list (carry unknown). Memory: one thread (stack) and a 4 KiB job ring. Line every 10 s
+  at resumes: "EDEN_UP_L1520_ASYNC_COPY: ... later lists copied on the GPUSnapshot thread, ...
+  copied here (queue full), ... waits".
+
+Changed from upstream: the copier sleeps on a std::condition_variable (not std::atomic::wait);
+the front list's entries already run were skipped here before (first_entry/first_word, the
+refresh check) and still are. Not ported: GpuSplit::semaphore_writes as a flat map (a type
+change that cannot be switched off); upstream's unit tests (src/tests is not built here).
+Read in source; not run.
+
+Unset (both): submitted_words allocates through ::operator new/delete as std::allocator did, no
+thread is started, and nothing else changes. No file here is a translation id input and no name
+is added to TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.
+
+(T182 merge: regenerated with git apply --3way on top of 0983-0985 (L1519/L1521); one hunk of gpu_thread.cpp moved by 0984 (L1521)'s lines, content unchanged.)
