+++ b/tools/eglantine-patches/0987-up-l1585-state-blocks.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,520 @@
+From: EglantinePS5
+Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_L1585_STATE_BLOCKS (zortos293/Lichii #1585, off unless set)
+
+Port of zortos293/Lichii #1585 (19ae2d1ebfb972d3011772d81b481e7309fed516, Zortos, co-author
+capy-ai; after Damfortx's state blocks 76548f0bf1 and stephenjayakar's StateDelta #641/#717):
+"send the split front's 3D state writes to the back as register blocks". Upstream's reason: the
+back replayed each changed 3D state register as its own ring entry (decode, method sink, shadow
+RAM, same-value check, deferred draw check, fast draw check, both dirty tables); in a Mario Kart
+World sample that was about 2.3 ms a frame on the back (PC). Not measured on the PS5.
+
+Against this tree: the ring already gathers plain state writes into one Regs entry with
+EDEN_PE_REG_BLOCKS=1 (ProsperoEden, off in play), but the back still sinks and processes them one
+by one (as Damfortx's version, which upstream found cut entries without cutting back time). What
+this adds is the part that saves back work: the front works out the dirty flags (OR of both
+tables) and the last write that ends EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW reuse, and the back stores the block at
+once.
+
+What (EDEN_UP_L1585_STATE_BLOCKS=1, only on top of the front's same-value skip):
+- Front (Maxwell3D::FrontWrite): a state write it sends (not in execution_mask, not a register a
+  back-run macro may own under EDEN_UP_L1056_BACK_MACROS, not in shadow RAM replay), from the
+  pushbuffer or a macro, goes into an open State entry in the ring (GpuSplit::StateWrite; the
+  open-entry mechanics of the Regs entry: at most 64 writes, closed before any other entry, a
+  publish or a drain). Entry: head (count, last breaking method), 4 words of dirty flags, then
+  method|value per write, in order.
+- Back (Maxwell3D::WriteStateRegisters): consumes the method sink, then stores the registers
+  (and the shadow RAM when tracked), sets the flags and breaks fast draw reuse once, when every
+  write changes its register, no deferred instanced draw is pending, no macro runs on the back,
+  no replay, and the write history, first-write trace and EDEN_NX2_GPU_PROFILE are off; else a
+  CallMethod of each write, as a direct write.
+- Ordering: a state write that used to wait in the back's method sink until the next executable
+  method now applies at its place in the stream (as a macro's direct write did, and as
+  EDEN_PE_REG_BLOCKS does). Upstream's NoteAnyWrite for blocks that may issue a deferred draw is
+  not needed here: this tree's front notes no draw as a guest memory writer.
+- EDEN_UP_L1585_STATE_BLOCKS_VERIFY=1 (upstream's EDEN_NX2_REG_BLOCK_VERIFY with both follow-up
+  fixes): each block also runs write by write from the same state, that result stays, and
+  registers, shadow RAM, dirty flags and the fast draw break are compared; an error line per
+  differing block (first 16) and a "EDEN_UP_L1585_STATE_BLOCKS_VERIFY" line every 10 s.
+- Count line every 10 s on the back: "EDEN_UP_L1585_STATE_BLOCKS in N s: ... blocks of ... writes
+  stored at once, ... one by one".
+Memory: none (the entries live in the existing 8 MiB ring; a State entry reserves 69 words).
+Not ported: upstream's unit test; EDEN_NX2_PERF_VERIFY / fast_maxwell3d conditions (not in this
+tree). With EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW's chain diagnostics a block counts one register break where the
+writes one by one counted one per write (counts only). Read in source; not run.
+
+Unset: nothing here runs (FrontState::state_blocks false). No file here is a translation id input
+and no name is added to TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.
+
